[00:02.5 --> 00:13.0]
SecretNAT is on by default -- it swaps your real secrets for reversible tokens before they reach the model. Only you can unmask them, locally.

[00:14.0 --> 00:25.0]
So grep what actually left the machine. Zero. The provider only ever saw a look-alike. It's NAT -- for secrets.
